    "why": "This is the tour’s pivot from close reading to reception within Scripture. The speakers explain that the passage is reused at least 27 times and that quotation reveals how later biblical authors understood it. In Numbers 14, Moses quotes not only “forgiving iniquity” but also the difficult line about not clearing the guilty—and then asks, “So forgive the people.” That surprising reuse challenges a purely negative reading of verse 7 and shows the passage functioning as an argument for mercy.",
